CloudBurrow patch 50 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1458). Applies after patch 0051; needs patches
0028 and 0036.

Patch 0036's change table of a table holds the table's columns but not
its pseudo-columns, so the change table of an ingestion-time partitioned
table (patch 0028) kept no _PARTITIONTIME: CloudBurrow's front could not
tell the partition of a change, so INFORMATION_SCHEMA.PARTITIONS'
last_modified_time ("the most recent time that data was written to the
partition") was NULL for every partition of such a table, and FOR
SYSTEM_TIME AS OF a past time of one was refused, its rows' partitions
unknown. The change table now keeps _PARTITIONTIME too, copied by the
triggers with the other columns, a pseudo-column of the change table as
of the table (SELECT * leaves it out). _PARTITIONDATE is the date of
_PARTITIONTIME and is not kept twice. A change table made before the
patch has no such column; the front reads its absence as before.
change_history_partition_time_test.go fails without the patch and passes
with it.

